# `iterate` is the READONLY walk: it declares a `.view` receiver, so it pins its
# container SHARED and other readers pass while the loop runs. Reading the map
# you are walking is the motivating case, and it works because the iterator says
# it only reads -- not because readers are exempt from locking. `iterateMut`
# still pins exclusively and still refuses this.
main: function is {
    m: (Map String value: String)
    m.set key: "a".string value: "x".string
    m.set key: "b".string value: "y".string
    with it: m.iterate do for k: it loop {
        v: m.get key: k.copy
        match (
            v
        ) case some then {
            print "k=\{k} v=\{v}"
        } case none then {
            print "k=\{k} missing"
        }
    }
}
